Title: Skill to initialize a project's decision log from its history
Created: 2026-11-25
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-11-25T15:21Z claude created

--- body ---
## Context

Filed from the replicator project (`~/CNRS/projets/actifs/replicator`) at
the author's request on 2026-11-25: "decision.log initialization: create a
harness skill". Replicator's `AGENTS.md` (commit e96e253) now names
`plans/decision.log` — "history of project key choices and their
rationale" — but the file does not exist. Writing it once by hand for one
project is the case a generic skill should serve instead (harness defines
skills and generic organization; projects define implementation).

## Request

A skill that initializes a project's decision log by mining what the
project already records: merge commits and commit bodies (the "why this
and not another" that `rules/git.md` asks for), plan/design files, closed
tickets. Each entry: date, decision, alternatives considered, rationale,
source reference (commit SHA, file, ticket). The output path and file
format are the caller's (replicator wants `plans/decision.log`); the skill
hardcodes neither.

## Premise checks for the receiver (Imagine)

- **Overlap with standing memory:** `rules/git.md` makes git the long-term
  memory and keeps history out of top-level files; roar captures journal
  entries under `memory/journal/`; smelt consolidates memory. Decide
  whether a decision log is a derived, regenerable view of git (fits the
  rule) or a second hand-maintained store (conflicts with it), and say so
  in the skill.
- **Init vs upkeep:** the request is initialization. Whether later entries
  come from the same skill on demand, from roar, or by hand is a design
  question to settle, not assume.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `skills/<name>/SKILL.md` builds a decision log from a project's git
      history, plans and tickets, every entry carrying a source reference.
- [ ] Output path and format come from the caller; nothing project-specific
      is hardcoded.
- [ ] The skill states its relation to `rules/git.md` § Git is the
      project's long-term memory, roar's journal and smelt.
- [ ] Trial on replicator produces `plans/decision.log`, landed by a
      replicator session.
